From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:54:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] DVDDemux: make the demuxer id counter atomic

Demuxers are created on the player thread and, through the DVDFileInfo
thumbnail and stream details jobs, on job threads at the same time.
The id counter they share is a plain static, so two demuxers can get
the same id and the stream lookup by demuxer id mixes them up.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemux.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemux.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemux.h
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemux.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemux.h
@@ -0,6 +0,7 @@
 #include "cores/FFmpeg.h"
 #include "utils/LanguageTag.h"
 
+#include <atomic>
 #include <chrono>
 #include <memory>
 #include <string>
@@ -0,7 +0,7 @@
 private:
   static int64_t NewGuid()
   {
-    static int64_t guid = 0;
+    static std::atomic<int64_t> guid{0};
     return guid++;
   }
 
